  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "The child is mapped as 'just trying to do my part'",
  "description": "The text 'just trying to do my part' is overlaid on the image of a severely malnourished child. This creates an analogical mapping where the child is implicitly identified as the entity performing the action described in the text — i.e., the child is being framed as if they are voluntarily participating in or contributing to a larger systemic issue, despite being a victim of extreme poverty and malnutrition. This mapping is harmful as it shifts blame from systemic causes to the child, portraying them as morally complicit in their own suffering.",
